{"availability":"available","full":"YusefSyed/callreclaim-webmcp","name":"callreclaim-webmcp","description":"A WebMCP missed-call desk where agents prepare replies and owners decide. Interactive demo with synthetic data.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-03T05:45:50Z","updated":"2026-09-29T02:45:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://callreclaim-agent-desk.yoosefseed.chatgpt.site","topics":["agentic-ai","human-in-the-loop","nextjs","openai","typescript","webmcp"],"demo":"https://callreclaim-agent-desk.yoosefseed.chatgpt.site/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:54.710Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:54.710Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:54.710Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:54.710Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CallReclaim is a synthetic missed-call desk for a business owner who has more requests than time. The owner says how many replies they can handle in the next 30 minutes. A WebMCP agent compares the inbox, cites the recorded facts, and stages a rescue plan. The owner must accept that plan before the agent can draft a reply.","The agent can prepare the work. It cannot approve or send it. There is no send tool and no messaging backend.","This repository is the isolated WebMCP Challenge edition. It contains no production CallReclaim infrastructure, customer records, phone numbers, credentials, external APIs, authentication, tracking, or messaging capability."],"features":["The owner sets a capacity of one or two replies for the next 30 minutes.","The agent lists the synthetic missed calls and reads the current owner brief.","The agent stages a rescue plan with exact fact citations for each selected lead.","The owner accepts or clears the plan manually.","The agent opens an accepted lead, stages an editable reply, and queues the current revision."],"sourceUrl"